  "content": {
    "title": "Everything you missed at the Oscars 2026: 'One Battle After Another' snags Best Picture, other top awards as 'Sinners' also wins big",
    "text": "Michael B. Jordan wins Best Actor for 'Sinners'By Page Six Team Winner: Michael B. Jordan, “Sinners” Michael B. Jordan accepting the Oscar for Best Actor for his role in \"Sinners.\" Getty Images Nominees: Timothée Chalamet, “Marty Supreme” Leonardo DiCaprio, “One Battle After Another” Ethan Hawke, “Blue Moon” Wagner Moura, “The Secret Agent” How to watch and stream Oscars Best Picture winner 'One Battle After Another'By Angela Tricarico Paul Thomas Anderson’s “One Battle After Another” secured Best Picture at the 2026 Oscars. Anderson also won for directing and adapted screenplay. The film follows Bob Ferguson (Leonardo DiCaprio) as he is drawn back into his past after his daughter goes missing. It also won Best Supporting Actor for Sean Penn. The cast of \"One Battle After Another\" celebrating after taking home the biggest award of the night. REUTERS READ MORE 'One Battle After Another' wins Best PictureBy Page Six Team Winner: “One Battle After Another” Director Paul Thomas Anderson and the cast of \"One Battle After Another\" on stage after winning Best Picture. Rob Latour/Shutterstock Nominees: “Marty Supreme” “Sentimental Value” “Bugonia” “F1” “Frankenstein” “Hamnet” “The Secret Agent” “Train Dreams” “Sinners” Jessie Buckley wins Best Actress for 'Hamnet'By Page Six Team Winner: Jessie Buckley, “Hamnet” Jessie Buckley accepting the Oscar for Best Actress for \"Hamnet.\" Getty Images Nominees: Rose Byrne, “If I Had Legs I’d Kick You” Kate Hudson, “Song Sung Blue” Renate Reinsve, “Sentimental Value” Emma Stone, “Bugonia” Paul Thomas Anderson wins Best Director for 'One Battle After Another'By Page Six Team Winner: Paul Thomas Anderson, “One Battle After Another” Paul Thomas Anderson accepting the Oscar for Best Director. AFP via Getty Images Nominees: Chloé Zhao, “Hamnet” Josh Safdie, “Marty Supreme” Ryan Coogler, “Sinners” Joachim Trier, “Sentimental Value” Autumn Durald Arkapaw makes Oscars history as first woman to win Best Cinematography Autumn Durald Arkapaw took home the Academy Award for Best Cinematography at the 2026 Oscars. The cinematographer won for her work on the horror action film, \"Sinners.\" Arkapaw made history, becoming the first woman and first black cinematographer to ever win this trophy. Autumn Durald Arkapaw (pictured here at the 2026 Oscars) made history being the first woman to win Best Cinematography. ABC \"I'm so honored to be here and I want all the women in the room to stand up,\" Arkapaw said in her acceptance speech as the audience erupted in applause. \"I don't feel like I'd get here without you guys.\" \"I have felt so much love from all the women on this whole campaign, and gotten to meet so many people and I just feel like moments like this happen because of you guys,” the winner continued. Javier Bardem tells Oscars crowd, 'No to war and free Palestine'By Kathleen Joyce Academy Award winner Javier Bardem took to the Oscars stage to present the award for Best International Film but had a message first before announcing the award. \"No to war and free Palestine,\" Bardem said into the microphone. Javier Bardem said \"free Palestine\" while presenting at the Oscar for Best International Film with Priyanka Chopra. REUTERS Bardem wore a pin at the Oscars that says, \"No to war\" in Spanish. Actress Priyanka Chopra was announcing the award with him. \"Sentimental Value\" won. Bardem wore a pin reading \"no to the war\" in Spanish. John Locher/Invision/AP Bardem has been outspoken about his views in the past. During the red carpet, when asked about his pin, Bardem said, \"The pin is about the same patch I wore in 2003 about the war in Iraq. And here we are 23 years after with another war led by Trump and Netanyahu and creating lots of damage and innocent being killed and bombed.\" 'Golden' from 'KPop Demon Hunters' wins Best SongBy Page Six Team Winner: “Golden” from “KPop Demon Hunters” Nominees: “Dear Me” from “Diane Warren: Relentless” “I Lied To You” from “Sinners” “Sweet Dreams of Joy” from “Viva Verdi!” “Train Dreams” from “Train Dreams” 'Sentimental Value' wins for Best International FeatureBy Page Six Team Winner: “Sentimental Value” Nominees: “The Secret Agent” “It Was Just An Accident” “Sirat” “The Voice of Hind Rajab” 'Bridesmaids' cast has a mini reunion at the 2026 Oscars By Alexandra Bellusci The cast of \"Bridesmaids\" appeared together at the 2026 Oscars, 15 years after the comedy first hit theaters. Kristen Wiig, Melissa McCarthy, Rose Byrne, Maya Rudolph and Ellie Kemper were on stage to present the award for Best Original Score. Before announcing \"Sinners\" as the winner, the ladies performed a hilarious bit for viewers by reading notes from audience members. Melissa Mccarthy, Rose Byrne, Kristen Wiig, Maya Rudolph and Ellie Kemper (pictured during the Oscars) have a mini \"Bridesmaids\" reunion. REUTERS \"'You're all aging well. Signed Stellan Skarsgård,'\" Rudolph read. \"This one is for me,\" Byrne chimed in. \"'Rose, can you please stop looking at me? The eye contact is too much. I'm thinking of leaving. Sincerely, Leonardo DiCaprio.'\" \"I apologize,\" the actress clapped back. \"I have been staring at you. I thought you were somebody else.\" McCarthy said it was \"almost impossible\" to read the handwriting on her note but did so anyways. \"'Hi, I'm with Stellan writing my own separate note. I also agree you women look radiant. All the things you've done to your faces look tasteful. Elle Fanning,'\" she read. \"'Just kidding. It's me again, Stellan Skarsgård.'\" \"'You guys have been talking for a long time. This bit could have been a lot shorter. This is really going on and on. That's all. Love you lots. Benicio del Toro. Or, for those of you who refuse to learn Spanish, it's Benedict of the bull,'\" Wigg shared. Lastly, Kemper rounded out the notes, reading, \"'I'm tired and I want to go home. This show is very long and there is no pizza. Signed the kid from 'Hamnet.''\" Ejae, Audrey Nuna and Rei Ami perform 'Golden' from 'KPop Demon Hunters' at OscarsBy Kathleen Joyce Ejae, Audrey Nuna and Rei Ami perform their hit song, \"Golden,\" from the Academy Award-winning film \"KPop Demon Hunters\" at the Oscars. Emma Stone claps along to \"Golden.\" ABC The hit song is nominated for the Best Original Song Oscar. The audience held up a K-pop light stick as the ladies performed the song. The flashlight-like device is meant to turn different colors during the song. 'Sinners' wins Best CinematographyBy Page Six Team Winner: “Sinners” Autumn Durald Arkapaw accepting the Oscar for Best Cinematography. Getty Images Nominees: “Frankenstein” “Marty Supreme” “One Battle After Another” “Train Dreams”",
